{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 30, :comments ["וַיַּרְא יִשְׂרָאֵל — at the shore of the sea. אֶת מִצְרַיִם — dead and drowning in the sea. עַל שְׂפַת הַיָּם — when Israel was at the shore of the sea, they immediately saw the sea return over the Egyptians and drown them in it; this is the essential plain sense. And on this matter I explained in Genesis: וַיִּשְׁמְעוּ אֶת קוֹל יְהוָה אֱלֹהִים מִתְהַלֵּךְ בַּגָּן לְרוּחַ הַיּוֹם."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {0 "The lemma from Genesis 3:8 is unaddressed in his text and left unaddressed here."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:41:32.163471531Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}